 "notes": "CardDemo's pending-authorization detail screen (transaction CPVD, program COPAUS1C, app-authorization-ims-db2-mq): pseudo-conversational. It schedules PSB PSBPAUTB (EXEC DLI SCHD), reads the selected authorization (GU the account's PAUTSUM0, GNP its PAUTDTL1 by key) and shows it, looking the decline reason up with SEARCH ALL; PF8 reads the next detail (GNP), PF5 toggles the fraud flag: it LINKs COPAUS2C (the Db2 fraud-report service, run here as the case's second program) and, when that succeeds, REPLaces the segment and takes a SYNCPOINT, else rolls back; PF3 XCTLs to COPAUS0C. The database is a small hand-stated one built from records of the corpus's own HD unload of DBPAUTP0 (accounts 1, 5, 11, 17; account 11 carries the authorization the Db2 seed already holds). Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own.",
